FILE task04-default-native-driver-design-c4/contracts/observer-proofs.md 
 # Closed observer and proof APIs

DESIGN signatures are finite; ACTUAL_PROOFS=[] remains EMPTY. No unsupported future extension is delegated to implementation. A missing proof returns unknown with explicit reason and fullK/STOP. Any added proof type/predicate/model/category requires a new design and independent review before installation.

```ts
type Decision<T> = {kind:"validated"; proofHash:H; value:T} |
 {kind:"unknown"; reason:"missing-evidence"|"unsupported"|"contradiction"|"bound-violation"};
interface ObservationContext { binding:BindingV2; scenarioId:CaseId; dispatchIdentity:H;
 enteredAt:Time; now:Time; originalDeadline:Time; sourceClosureHash:H }
interface InputGenerate { ctx:ObservationContext; result:LanguageModelV4GenerateResult;
 nativeRequestCanonical:string; privateText:string }
interface InputStream { ctx:ObservationContext; events:ObservedEvent[];
 privateText:string; ended:"reader-done"|"abort"|"deadline"|"error" }
interface InputEmbed { ctx:ObservationContext; result:EmbeddingModelV4Result;
 nativeRequestCanonical:string }
function observeGenerate(x:InputGenerate, proofs:ClosedResolver):ReceiptV2;
function observeStream(x:InputStream, proofs:ClosedResolver):ReceiptV2;
function observeEmbed(x:InputEmbed, proofs:ClosedResolver):ReceiptV2;
function verifyAtCapture(receipt:ReceiptV2, prior:Facts|null,
 ctx:ObservationContext, proofs:ClosedResolver, backing:VerificationBacking):ReceiptV2;
```

Inputs are exclusively official v4 result objects/chunks plus compiled private data; no fetch injection or caller truth/proof args. Detach bounded own-data objects before read. Headers/request bodies/reasoning never persist in public receipts. Observer raw working memory <=180000 UTF8 canonical bytes, <=4096nodes/depth16, <=512 stream events, <=8 raw usage-bearing chunks, <=1 native finish; reject oversize before allocating further retained observation. No qualified evidence from clipped buffers. Append digest can be computed incremental over complete serial raw/native event canonical sequence while discarding private raw after observation; private text itself <=conditional case bound. Reasoning/tool/nontext content yields unsupported/private-withhold. This envelope is an engineering STOP, not a provider theorem.

### Generate predicates

Require official result response.body is detached own raw object, raw choices array length1/index0, raw id/model valid ID; choice.message.content is scalar well-formed text, no tool_calls/function_call/reasoning/refusal content admitted. Raw finish exactly stop|length|content_filter and native finish unified/raw exact map/raw. Native response.id/modelId, if present, must equal raw id/model. Never use requested model instance ID as serving evidence. Join all native text content exactly in order and require equality raw content/privateText; any other native content unsupported. Raw usage prompt_tokens/completion_tokens safe N and native mapped inputTokens.total/outputTokens.total safe equal counts establish usage only; missing raw fields remain null even if converter reports0. Presence of conflicting total_tokens, if supplied, yields contradiction unless exact input+output safe sum. Native raw count detail/cache fields remain root-private; money resolver examines exact raw usage categories/source semantics separately. Returned generation alone nominates terminal; only matching lifetimeProof validates it. Raw/model mismatch marks drift before attach; mismatch does not erase genuinely supported terminal or independently covered money.

### Ordered stream reducer

ObservedEvent is exact {sequence:N, kind:"raw"|"response-metadata"|"text-delta"|"text-start"|"text-end"|"finish"|"error"|"unsupported", digest:H, data:unknown}; sequence starts0 contiguous. Reducer reads only detached supported native events; unsupported original types are recorded as kind unsupported and STOP. One reader consumes native stream, no tee/observer loop. Every raw id/model must match the first supplied id/model verbatim; changing either => contradiction. Raw chunks choices length1/index0 while content/finish is present; usage-only tail may choices[]. Each text delta exact scalar, cumulative bounded native text corresponds exactly raw choice.delta.content sequence (each raw data chunk paired with derived native events by serial order). No normalized text reconstruction. At most one distinct raw finish for choice0; repeats identical raw finish/ID facts permitted only on same raw source duplicate? Frozen choice: any SECOND raw finish-bearing chunk => contradiction, even equal, to avoid invented terminal aggregation. Usage raw fields across <=8 chunks may be absent then supplied; once any count/cost/category field supplied, differing later value => contradiction. Required terminal is observed raw finish + stable ID/model + one native finish after that raw finish and after final native text-end; native finish raw/unified must match. Native finish generated by flush with no raw finish is unknown, NEVER trusted terminal. Content/choice chunks after raw finish => contradiction; a usage-only tail is allowed before final native finish. reader-done before native finish/raw terminal unknown; abort/deadline/error unknown unless genuine full terminal had already been reduced (then retain terminal facts). In all cases local endings do not fabricate zero money. Flush nominal finish by itself is not independent upstream lifetime evidence.

### Embedding predicates

Official result response.body rawValue is required for correlation. Minimal upstream accepted response schema validates only data/embedding and optional usage.prompt_tokens/providerMetadata, not id/model. Require data length1, mapped embeddings length1, each raw embedding exactly mapped finite1536 numbers (no -0), profile exact. Raw id/model, when actually supplied, are parsed verbatim ID; missing either means terminal/serving unknown. Never make an ID from dispatch hash, vector hash or mapped modelId. Raw response optional usage.prompt_tokens equals mapped usage.tokens safe N yields usage input; no observed embedding output token counter inferred: semantic mapped/raw output0 is only for the no-generated-token embedding contract source proof; before that receipt output counts null and usage may remain unknown if proof absent. A native successful promise is only a nomination. Resolver must contain accepted terminal rule successful-single-vector-response-id-model-v1 for the exact source/serving model and correlation to returned body. No such actual proof exists now, so even successful valid vector + usage emits unknown lifetime/money/serving/fullK/STOP. Malformed or unsupported raw/body/vector yields unknown/STOP and withheld result.

## Exact closed proof registry

```ts
interface ProofCommon { version:1; proofHash:H; type:"lifetime"|"serving"|"money";
 installationHash:H; reviewerAcceptanceHash:H; validatorSourceHash:H;
 providerSourceHash:H; providerVersion:"0.2.1"; adapterVersion:"3.0.14";
 providerV4Version:"4.0.21"; loadedClosureHash:H; sourceRevision:H;
 checkedAt:Time; expiresAt:Time; targetHash:H; manifestHash:H;
 requestedModel:Model; actualModels:ID[]; methods:Method[] }
interface LifetimeProof extends ProofCommon { type:"lifetime";
 rule:"chat-correlated-raw-native-finish-v1"|"successful-single-vector-response-id-model-v1";
 supportsRawFinish:["stop","length","content_filter"]|[];
 confirmsWholeInvocationTermination:true }
interface ServingProof extends ProofCommon { type:"serving";
 exactObservedModel:ID; immutableRevision:ID; tokenizerArtifact:H;
 framingProof:H; capProof:H; decoderProof:H; nativePrivateCorrespondenceProof:H;
 boundsRevision:H; inputUCap:N; outputMCap:N; privateMaximumBytes:N }
interface MoneyProof extends ProofCommon { type:"money";
 extraction:"raw-usage-cost-v1"; currency:"USD";
 aggregate:"complete-whole-invocation-account-charge";
 categories:["cache-read","cache-write","cancelled","inference","rejected","routing","surcharge"];
 coversAllAttempts:true; coversDriftModels:ID[]; rejectedAndCancelledChargeRule:H;
 cacheAndRoutingChargeRule:H; currencySemanticProof:H; wholeInvocationProof:H;
 rateRevision:H; categorySemanticProof:H }
interface ClosedResolver {
 lifetime(ctx,nomination:TerminalNomination):Decision<true>;
 serving(ctx,rawModel:ID|null):Decision<ServingProof>;
 money(ctx,facts:MoneyNomination):Decision<{microUSD:N; currency:"USD"; categories:Category[]}> }
```

All exact own keys with Receipt graph constraints, proof <=8192bytes; actualModels/coversDriftModels sorted unique valid IDs max16, methods sorted unique <=3; checkedAt<expiresAt, lifetime rule interface-specific. Accepted registry includes exact proof content hash, source hashes/review acceptance pin and root-only installation hash; no arbitrary valid-shaped proof is accepted. ACTUAL_PROOFS constant empty frozen array in design sample; root cannot install via run/capture/public mutation or caller ref. Later root stages exact finite records only after fresh evidence/review/current-source/native gates and frozen operator manifest review; registry is compiled server-private, constructor closes over it. Observer selects by exact ctx loadedClosure/target/manifest/requested model/method and raw actual model inclusion, no caller selection. Capture reruns same resolver against dispatch-bound sanitized nominations/raw digest retained privately; receipt label/reference alone never qualifies. If raw backing evidence unavailable to capture, unknown/STOP (no digest-as-provider-attestation).

Dispatch rechecks now in [checkedAt,expiresAt), current installation/source/load hash and target epochs before reserve/entry. Historical capture requires proof valid at enteredAt and exact historical dispatch/source binding; current expiry/revocation closes delivery/future dispatch but does not rewrite qualified historical charge. A proof cryptographically/source revoked for invalid evidence is NOT historical valid and returns unknown; previously committed charge remains immutable until separately reviewed explicit accounting correction, never automatic refund. serving rule additionally requires exact requested raw model equality; documented alias/snapshot source proof cannot normalize a mismatch. money may cover exact drift actualModel only when in both actualModels and coversDriftModels and complete coverage proves all categories. Observed rejected/cancelled/cache/routing cost needs explicit complete proof even if the main request had no tools. Absence of categories does not prove none; unknown category or missing whole-invocation evidence returns unknown. No direct OpenRouter lookup, unsupported currency assertion, tariff inference, dependency hack or fallback.

## Exact monetary conversion

Pin reviewed runtimeGateway.ts SHA e796e43aafe70c37d8af7330a969e5b643eb58e86be7621cc7c08991ff1224be conservativeUsdDecimal lines179–196. Design example duplicates only its pure arithmetic, never imports governed production root. Decimal strings accepted /^\d+(?:\.\d+)?$/ <=80 remain exact; convert to rational BigInt numerator/10^scale, outward ceil(numerator*1000000/denominator); reject result>MAX_SAFE_INTEGER. IEEE numeric positive uses bitwise next representable upper adjacent then exact rational outward microceil; -0/negative/nonfinite/overflow invalid; numeric0 ->0. Store exact resulting decimal and micro integer together. A positive numeric cost exactly at a micro boundary conservatively rounds above it; do not use Math.round/toFixed/float multiplication. This is amount conversion only: empty resolver still returns unknown even on valid0. Entire full accepted cost is charged once above K/$10; no clipping, no guessed token-derived amount.

## Nomination types and deterministic resolver procedure

```ts
type Model=ReceiptV2["requestedModel"]; type Method=ReceiptV2["method"];
interface TerminalNomination {method:Method;responseId:ID|null;actualModel:ID|null;
 rawFinish:ReceiptV2["rawFinish"];nativeFinish:ReceiptV2["nativeFinish"];
 nativeRawFinish:ID|null;correlatedShape:boolean;rawDigest:H;
 transcriptRef:H; // private observer store content-addressed reference, not public truth
 ended:"returned"|"reader-done"|"abort"|"deadline"|"error"}
interface MoneyNomination {method:Method;responseId:ID|null;actualModel:ID|null;
 rawCost:string|number|null;rawCurrency:ID|null;observedCategories:Category[];
 outcome:"returned"|"rejected"|"cancelled"|"unknown";
 rawDigest:H;transcriptRef:H}
```

correlatedShape is only reducer's nomination, not an authority label: capture reloads bounded private transcript by transcriptRef, recomputes digest and reducer predicates before calling closed resolver. Transcript cache is fixture-owned private ephemeral/durable staging/evidence, keyed dispatch+rawDigest with bounded180000bytes and max1first+2refinements; if lost/absent return missing-evidence. Add optional fixtureEvidence table exact {dispatchIdentity:H,rawDigest:H,privateTranscriptCanonical:string,createdAt:Time}, by_dispatch_digest index [dispatchIdentity,rawDigest]. It holds only bounded provider evidence, not account/charge/permit truth. Root cleanup hashes it before removal. All access internal, no public get/read. Semantic validator parses provider transcript using exact supported surface predicates, rejects unknown required terminal shapes but may retain unrecognized raw fields privately for category completeness review. Never stringify full response headers/JWT/prompt into it; raw provider chunks/text may be private.

Resolver procedure for all3 methods: (1) recompute transcript/predicate; (2) find unique compiled installed proof whose exact hash/review/source/install binding matches dispatch context; >1matching proof contradiction; no match missing-evidence; (3) historical/currentness rules above; (4) specific rule's exact actualModels/method/terminal or serving or monetary coverage predicates; (5) return validated bound value or unknown reason. No proof can be installed because a receipt shaped correctly. No raw currency field is required if independently accepted currencySemanticProof establishes raw usage.cost is aggregateUSD for this invocation, but ReceiptV2 observedCurrency="USD" must then be explicitly resolver-established classification with provenance (not a claimed raw string). Field name observedCurrency records supported semantic observation, not necessarily raw literal; rawCurrency nomination stays nullable. Actual registry EMPTY means no USD classification is established now.

Rejected invocation/provider error with absent supported correlated raw ID/model/terminal remains unknown lifetime; MoneyNomination outcome rejected/cancelled may be known ONLY if private supported raw response cost and installed proof cover that full invocation/category/actual model. No error object fabrication/refetch. Cancellation is local control and does not by itself nominate cancelled upstream outcome; only supported provider evidence can set that outcome, otherwise unknown.

## Experiment entry source currentness versus actual proof currentness

The experiment does NOT require ACTUAL_PROOFS nonempty to reserve/enter its first investigation: that would falsely apply production bootstrap to unknown premises. Entry uses a separately compiled conditional source snapshot EXACT {version:1,manifestHash:H,targetHash:H,loadedClosureHash:H,providerSourceHash:H,adapterSourceHash:H,providerV4TypesHash:H,modelDocumentHash:H,tokenizerArtifactHash:H,framingProofHash:H,outputProofHash:H,rateDocumentHash:H,boundRevision:H,priceRevision:H,checkedAt:Time,expiresAt:Time,hypothesis:true}. Snapshot is root-installed only in the independently reviewed fixture manifest; every hash/source revision current and checkedAt<=now<expiresAt before reserve/immediate enter. It records accepted conditional U/M/K/output source premises, NEVER actual serving/decoder/aggregate monetary qualification. Account proofCurrent means this hypothesis source snapshot is current; actual resolver EMPTY still permits bounded experiment entry but returns unknown after observations, latching STOP/fullK/withheld results. Already-qualified production governed dispatch remains a separate actual-proof gate. Source expiry prevents future experiment entry without silently renewing the original window/account; no renewal/reset is permitted.

C3 private fixtureEvidence rows additionally carry immutable accountHash,targetHash,operatorHash,manifestHash; ROOT hash-only recovery/purge per replay-cleanup.md is permitted after inference closure. All observation/proof predicates and EMPTY actual registry remain unchanged.

C4 VerificationBacking exact retained|transient union in hash-recovery.md allows independently supported late original-account refinements after private purge without persisting private tables again. All closed resolver/EMPTY actual proof predicates remain identical; missing/unsupported backing remains unknown. Immutable trigger T cannot be changed by capture.

FILE task04-default-native-driver-implementation-c2/design-clarification-c3/money-domain.md 
 # Present finite money domain and future extraction gate

Current exact frozen observer→closed-money admissible domain is EMPTY: official reviewed observer predicates define raw usage.cost and token counts but no exact category extraction schema. Therefore observedCategories=[] and closed createResolver.money must return UNKNOWN/missing-evidence; cost0 is not qualified zero. Capture reruns observer and preserves UNKNOWN/fullK/STOP. Do not copy diagnostic raw usage.categories, infer inference, accept caller categories/proof, or amend actual registry EMPTY. Mock-resolver full-money positives remain conditional algebra tests, not supported closed pipeline proof. This is an explicit unresolved actual-money pipeline/qualification blocker for ultimate Task04, not removal of required functionality.

Before ANY positive observer-money admissions a separately reviewed finite source-evidence extraction contract must provide: exact official provider/adapter/type source SHA+locations/version; method-specific supported raw result/chunk paths; exact own-data field/type/scalar categories schema; sorted enum/duplicate/conflict/unknown semantics; completeness across cache-read/cache-write/cancelled/inference/rejected/routing/surcharge and all attempts; correlation to raw ID/model/dispatch; usage-tail ordering; rejected/cancelled evidence without inferred local outcome; amount/currency semantic provenance; drift coverage; capture transcript revalidation. A hash-only categorySemanticProof without its exact predicate is insufficient. The future interface remains module-private extractMoneyNomination(ctx, verifiedTranscript, compiledAcceptedCategorySemantics), returning UNKNOWN(reason) or exact immutable categories bound to rawDigest/transcriptRef and actual raw amount/currency. It accepts no public label or proof choice. Until concrete official supported bytes and predicate pass independent design+source gates, only UNKNOWN is admissible. No present synthetic schema is asserted to be official.

